Package: evanxlsx
Type: Package
Title: Simple Consistent Excel Exports
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Evan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "104670239+lianglunping@users.noreply.github.com")
Author: Evan [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Evan <104670239+lianglunping@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Exports data frames to Excel using 'openxlsx2', with consistent
    formatting and explicit file protection. Optional 'polars' helpers provide
    numeric summaries, non-destructive interquartile-range flags, strict text
    splitting and key validation through Tidy column selection. Does not
    upload data or install packages during use. Existing exports do not
    require the optional data-processing dependencies.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.3)
Imports: openxlsx2 (>= 1.29)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.2.0),
    xml2,
    tibble,
    dplyr (>= 1.1.0),
    duckplyr (>= 1.2.1),
    polars (>= 1.16.0),
    rlang (>= 1.1.0),
    tidyselect (>= 1.2.0),
    tidypolars (>= 0.19.0),
    tidyr,
    stringr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: A zip utility supported by openxlsx2
